    "text": "- 2024-09-30 — Treasury’s fiscal-year-end federal debt report shows the “Total Federal Debt and Interest Payable” figure, and the report notes that the average interest rate on the nonmarketable balance is calculated excluding inflation-indexed securities from the average-rate calculation. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/frusg/FRUSG_2024.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/frusg/FRUSG_2024.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2024-09-30 — In Treasury’s audited FY 2024 federal debt schedule, the average interest rate on Treasury Inflation-Protected Securities (TIPS) was 0.7% and on Treasury Floating Rate Notes (FRNs) was 4.7% for the debt held by the public section. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/frusg/FRUSG_2024.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/frusg/FRUSG_2024.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2024-09-30 — Treasury Fiscal Data’s “Historical Debt Outstanding” dataset states that total debt outstanding is reported as of fiscal year end, and that the federal fiscal year runs from October 1 to September 30. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-07-31 — Treasury’s monthly “Schedules of Federal Debt” reports the average interest rate on Intragovernmental Debt Holdings without TIPS and FRNs as 3.1%. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-07-31 — Treasury’s monthly “Schedules of Federal Debt” reports the average interest rate on Intragovernmental FRNs as 4.3%. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-07-31 — Treasury’s monthly “Schedules of Federal Debt” states that the nonmarketable balance includes inflation-indexed securities that are excluded from the average interest rate calculation. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202507.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\nI did not find a Treasury Fiscal Data page specifically dated 2026-09-30; the most recent official Treasury Fiscal Data results available in the search were through mid-2025, so I reported the nearest relevant primary-source findings instead. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai))"
