    "title": "Fiscal Data Average Interest Rate Amount Interest-bearing Debt Total Interest-bearing Debt September 2026",
    "published": null,
    "text": "- 2025-05-31 — Treasury Fiscal Data’s **Monthly Statement of the Public Debt** dataset is published monthly and includes a table with **average interest rate** and **total interest-bearing debt** fields for Treasury securities outstanding. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-06-17 — Treasury Fiscal Data’s **Debt to the Penny** dataset reports **total public debt outstanding** daily and defines it as the sum of **intragovernmental holdings** and **debt held by the public**. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/debt-to-the-penny/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/debt-to-the-penny/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-09-30 — Treasury Fiscal Data’s **Historical Debt Outstanding** dataset is annual and covers fiscal years ending on **September 30**; the federal fiscal year runs from **October 1 to September 30**. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/historical-debt-outstanding/?utm_source=openai))\n- 2025-09-30 — Treasury Fiscal Data indicates the **Monthly Statement of the Public Debt** is published on the **fourth business day of each month**, with figures showing the debt as of the **end of the previous month**. Source: https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/ ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai))\n\nI could not verify a **September 2026** publication yet from the official Fiscal Data sources available in search results, so I’m not claiming any September 2026 figures."
