    "text": "- **2026-09-30** — I could not verify a published Treasury source for the **September 30, 2026** Monthly Statement / average interest rate / total interest-bearing debt yet; the Treasury Fiscal Data MSPD dataset currently shown on its site only goes through **2025-05-31** in the accessible dataset page I found, and TreasuryDirect points to the current-month average interest rates page rather than a September 2026 public-debt statement. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai)) — **Source URL:** https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/ ; https://www.treasurydirect.gov/government/public-debt-reports/average-monthly-interest/ ; https://www.treasurydirect.gov/government/public-debt-reports/debt-position-and-activity-report/\n\n- **2025-05-31** — Treasury Fiscal Data’s **Schedules of Federal Debt** monthly report shows the outstanding federal debt categories and notes that the report is **unaudited** for the month; the report includes principal balances for debt held by the public and intragovernmental debt holdings, with average interest-rate note text for intragovernmental holdings. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf?utm_source=openai)) — **Source URL:** https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/static-data/published-reports/schedules-fed-debt-monthly/SchedulesFederalDebt_Monthly_202505.pdf\n\n- **2025-05-31** — TreasuryDirect’s **Average Interest Rates on U.S. Treasury Securities** page states that the averages for **Total Marketable, Total Nonmarketable, and Total Interest-bearing Debt** do **not include TIPS and FRNs**; this is the official page to use for current-month average interest rates. ([treasurydirect.gov](https://www.treasurydirect.gov/government/public-debt-reports/average-monthly-interest/?utm_source=openai)) — **Source URL:** https://www.treasurydirect.gov/government/public-debt-reports/average-monthly-interest/\n\n- **2025-06-05** — Treasury Fiscal Data’s MSPD dataset page says the data are published **monthly** and are **“detailing the debt as of the end of the previous month”**; that means the closest official monthly statement to a fiscal date like September 30 is usually the report published in early October, but I did **not** find a September 30, 2026 publication yet. ([fiscaldata.treasury.gov](https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/?utm_source=openai)) — **Source URL:** https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-statement-public-debt/\n\nIf you want, I can do a second pass focused specifically on finding the exact **September 2026** Treasury PDF or dataset row once it is published, and extract the precise **average interest rate** and **total interest-bearing debt**."
